Lane Warden Production Battle Slice
Build: P2-0.17.1
Design baseline: 1.7
Stable install scope: /lol-the-spire/lane-warden-prod-v0.10.4/
P2-0.17.1 touch fix: worksite acquisition now uses a minimum 84px-diameter screen-space target at overview zoom, covering the miniature, its label, and the usable side of sites near the ability rail.
Split Causeway regression coverage now routes the Warden to all four worksites and verifies that construction can be committed at each destination.
P2 Strategic Fieldworks: four fixed off-lane worksites add irreversible battle commitments without changing deployment legality or reward packet structure.
Fieldwork plans: Tower Emplacement costs 32g and 8s for autonomous local fire; Muster Camp costs 38g and 9s to relocate controlled scheduled reinforcements; Field Relay costs 28g and 7s to shorten its paired cut-through by 22%.
Commander commitment: the Warden physically approaches a selected site, loses Presence while off-lane or working, may leave at any time, and retains paid construction progress for a later return.
Living battlefield: vertical world space is 38% taller, with build clearings and spur roads above and below the two organic lanes. The default overview retains both lanes while close zoom preserves full model scaling.
Breach flow: a destroyed Guard no longer remains the friendly formation cap. Cohorts stream through and compress into a visible Gate assault rather than attacking from behind the old breach line.
Compatibility: existing P2 saves initialize fieldworks lazily. Combat balance, scheduled pulse totals, deployment capacity, reward packets, progression, Reclamation, and Last Stand remain otherwise unchanged.
P2-0.15.1 delivery protections remain: explicit shell build marker, mixed-shell repair, stale-shell rejection, and build.json-last deployment discipline.
